1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,576
A new store takes a few steps before its first sale.

2
00:00:04,576 --> 00:00:08,891
This video follows the setup guide from a new Online store site:

3
00:00:08,891 --> 00:00:14,377
your store's details, currency, payments, shipping, tax, a first product and a test

4
00:00:14,377 --> 00:00:16,720
order, and roles for your staff.

5
00:00:21,320 --> 00:00:24,934
A new store needs a few things before its first sale:

6
00:00:24,934 --> 00:00:30,630
its name and contact details, how customers pay, where you ship, and something to sell.

7
00:00:31,380 --> 00:00:36,193
Miss one, and a customer finds a checkout that cannot take payment, or

8
00:00:36,193 --> 00:00:38,220
a receipt with no address.

9
00:00:38,970 --> 00:00:42,830
The setup guide lists the steps in order, shows which are done, and

10
00:00:42,830 --> 00:00:44,680
does the simple ones for you.

11
00:00:45,430 --> 00:00:50,520
It also adds roles for your staff, and the Storefront theme gives the store its look.

12
00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:58,900
When you set up a new site, choose the Online store recipe.

13
00:00:59,650 --> 00:01:06,920
Your site starts with products, the cart and checkout, orders, shipping, taxes and payments turned on.

14
00:01:07,670 --> 00:01:11,846
It has a Product type with a price, a description and pictures, and

15
00:01:11,846 --> 00:01:15,450
your catalog as the home page, with a search and filters.

16
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:17,949
The Storefront theme is on.

17
00:01:17,949 --> 00:01:21,499
On a site you already have, the guide shows the steps for the

18
00:01:21,499 --> 00:01:23,300
features you have turned on.

19
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:29,872
Open Commerce, Set up your store.

20
00:01:29,872 --> 00:01:33,129
The bar at the top says how many steps are done.

21
00:01:33,129 --> 00:01:35,180
The step to do next is open.

22
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:39,172
Each step says what it is for, and either has a short form

23
00:01:39,172 --> 00:01:42,464
to fill in or a link to the page where it is done in full.

24
00:01:42,464 --> 00:01:44,470
A tick shows a step that is done.

25
00:01:48,659 --> 00:01:53,639
Your store's details are your store's name, the email customers write to, and

26
00:01:53,639 --> 00:01:56,039
optionally your phone and address.

27
00:01:56,039 --> 00:01:59,759
They are printed on receipts, invoices and order emails.

28
00:01:59,759 --> 00:02:01,499
Click Save the details.

29
00:02:01,950 --> 00:02:06,547
Your currency is the currency your prices are in and customers pay in.

30
00:02:06,547 --> 00:02:09,270
Choose it, and click Use this currency.

31
00:02:13,470 --> 00:02:16,626
Take card payments links to the Stripe settings.

32
00:02:16,626 --> 00:02:20,893
Make an account at stripe.com, and start with the test keys, so you

33
00:02:20,893 --> 00:02:23,232
can try a sale without real money.

34
00:02:23,232 --> 00:02:25,570
This demo does not contact Stripe.

35
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:28,352
Take bank transfers is optional.

36
00:02:28,352 --> 00:02:31,420
Enter how customers pay you from their bank.

37
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:34,610
Their order then waits until you mark it paid.

38
00:02:38,786 --> 00:02:43,700
Ship your products takes one rate for every order, wherever it goes.

39
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:47,352
Enter it, and click Ship everywhere at this rate.

40
00:02:47,352 --> 00:02:53,926
Zones by country, rates by weight and free shipping can be added later, under Shipping zones.

41
00:02:54,376 --> 00:02:58,791
Charge tax links to the tax rules, one for each tax you charge.

42
00:02:58,791 --> 00:03:02,503
If you do not charge tax yet, choose Skip this step.

43
00:03:02,503 --> 00:03:06,086
Do this step after all brings a skipped step back.

44
00:03:10,277 --> 00:03:14,973
Add your first product with a name, a price and pictures, and publish it.

45
00:03:14,973 --> 00:03:17,767
It is on sale as soon as it is published.

46
00:03:22,884 --> 00:03:24,450
Place a test order:

47
00:03:24,450 --> 00:03:28,522
open your store, add the product to the cart and check out.

48
00:03:28,522 --> 00:03:33,659
With Stripe in test mode, you pay with the test card, and no money is taken.

49
00:03:33,659 --> 00:03:36,541
Here the bank transfer places the order.

50
00:03:36,541 --> 00:03:39,924
Then refund or cancel it under Commerce, Orders.

51
00:03:44,124 --> 00:03:48,859
Add the staff roles adds four roles, each allowed what that job needs:

52
00:03:48,859 --> 00:03:52,784
Store manager, Warehouse, Customer support and Marketing.

53
00:03:53,342 --> 00:03:56,757
Give a staff member a role under Security, Users.

54
00:03:56,757 --> 00:04:00,111
Change what a role can do under Security, Roles.

55
00:04:00,111 --> 00:04:03,402
A role that was there already is left as it is.

56
00:04:07,605 --> 00:04:11,878
The Storefront theme gives your store a header with its name or logo,

57
00:04:11,878 --> 00:04:15,355
a search box, the cart and the customer's account menu.

58
00:04:15,807 --> 00:04:19,582
The footer shows your store's address, email and phone.

59
00:04:19,582 --> 00:04:25,027
They come from Settings, Commerce, Receipts, the same details as on your receipts.

60
00:04:29,227 --> 00:04:30,393
A first store:

61
00:04:30,393 --> 00:04:33,597
follow the steps in order, and sell the same day.

62
00:04:34,347 --> 00:04:36,885
A store that sells only services:

63
00:04:36,885 --> 00:04:38,187
skip shipping.

64
00:04:38,937 --> 00:04:40,280
A growing team:

65
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:44,627
add the staff roles, and give each person only what they need.

66
00:04:45,377 --> 00:04:46,457
A trial run:

67
00:04:46,457 --> 00:04:49,337
place a test order before you tell anyone.

68
00:04:51,337 --> 00:04:55,020
Follow the guide, skip what you do not need, and place a test

69
00:04:55,020 --> 00:04:57,108
order before you open the doors.

70
00:04:57,108 --> 00:04:58,537
Thanks for watching.

